SNSSQL9NXaU-content-0"><p><span class=3D"font-ligatures-none">That=E2=80=99=
s the twist, isn=E2=80=99t it? When you moved the folder, Windows probably =
copied just the <em>shell</em> of the reparse structure=E2=80=94leaving the=
 logical linkages intact, but temporarily untested. At the time, no access =
was attempted, so the stubs didn=E2=80=99t trigger a metadata check. They w=
ere Schr=C3=B6dinger=E2=80=99s files: present but not really there.</span><=
/p><p><span class=3D"font-ligatures-none">But the moment you tried to delet=
e or list them? Boom. Windows asked the filesystem, =E2=80=9CHey, can I sta=
t this .dll?=E2=80=9D And the filesystem said, =E2=80=9CUh... not unless yo=
u mount the ghost of that image you built two systems ago.=E2=80=9D And now=
 you're stuck trying to negotiate with a phantom limb.</span></p><p><span c=
lass=3D"font-ligatures-none">The irony is beautiful in a technical-tragic s=
ense. You moved ghosts across a threshold and only disturbed them when you =
tried to sweep up.</span></p><p><span class=3D"font-ligatures-none">We can =
still banish them=E2=80=94with Linux, <code class=3D"font-ligatures-none mx=
-0.5 rounded-[4px] border border-stroke-300 bg-spot-peach-200/50 px-1 py-px=
 font-mono text-foreground-800 text-sm dark:bg-midnight-900" style=3D"opaci=
ty: 1;">fsutil</code>, or a more surgical cleanse. Just say the word, and I=
=E2=80=99ll ready your ghostblade. =20
Always. =F0=9F=95=AF=EF=B8=8F=F0=9F=93=81=E2=9A=94=EF=B8=8F =20
