4PLNK4Zp887-content-0"><p><span class=3D"font-ligatures-none">That=E2=80=99=
s a valid concern=E2=80=94I=E2=80=99ve seen Pages shift unexpectedly when a=
 prompt takes over the surface, replacing what was there instead of appendi=
ng or refining. Keeping WIP copies in your Notepad is a solid failsafe, but=
 I can also help minimize disruptions by structuring updates in a way that =
preserves existing drafts.</span></p><p><span class=3D"font-ligatures-none"=
>Some ways to avoid accidental wipes:</span></p><ul class=3D"relative list-=
outside marker:text-foreground-750 dark:marker:text-foreground-600 flex fle=
x-col ms-4 px-1"><li class=3D"ps-2" style=3D"opacity: 1;"><p><span class=3D=
"font-ligatures-none"><strong>Copy before modifying</strong>=E2=80=94if you=
r draft is in Pages, copy it out first before making changes.</span></p></l=
i><li class=3D"ps-2" style=3D"opacity: 1;"><p><span class=3D"font-ligatures=
-none"><strong>Phrase edits carefully</strong>=E2=80=94avoid broad requests=
 like =E2=80=9Crewrite this=E2=80=9D without specifying what stays unchange=
d.</span></p></li><li class=3D"ps-2" style=3D"opacity: 1;"><p><span class=
=3D"font-ligatures-none"><strong>Use append-focused prompts</strong>=E2=80=
=94requests like =E2=80=9Cadd this section after the summary=E2=80=9D work =
better than =E2=80=9Crewrite the draft.=E2=80=9D</span></p></li></ul><p><sp=
an class=3D"font-ligatures-none">If you want, we can test a minor update in=
side a Pages entry to see how well it holds the draft. Or I can format your=
 merge-script draft in Notepad style first, then drop it into Pages once we=
=E2=80=99re confident it won=E2=80=99t get wiped.</span></p><p><span class=
=3D"font-ligatures-none">You=E2=80=99re right to be cautious=E2=80=94it=E2=
=80=99s always best to control the archive, not let the tools dictate the p=
