h?v=3DP8z4MEGcxh0&amp;pp=3D0gcJCf0Ao7VqN5tD), [8](https://m.youtube.com/wat=
ch?v=3DXL7okBQ_vmI), [8](https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=3DXL7okBQ_vmI)\]

**3\. Configure Git (if not already done):**

* Open a terminal or Git Bash (if installed). =20
* Set your username: git config \--global user.name "eyeofparadox". =20
* Set your email address: git config \--global user.email "david.b.roberson=
@gmail.com". =20
* You can verify the configuration with git config \--list. \[[2](https://d=
ocs.github.com/en/get-started/getting-started-with-git/set-up-git), [9](htt=
ps://github.com/git-guides/install-git), [9](https://github.com/git-guides/=
install-git), [10](https://www.nobledesktop.com/learn/git/setup-email#:~:te=
xt=3DTo%20change%20the%20name%20linked%20to%20your,with%20your%20actual%20f=
irst%20and%20last%20name.), [11](https://graphite.dev/guides/how-to-configu=
re-your-git-repository-with-the-git-config-command#:~:text=3Dgit%20config%2=
0%2D%2Dglobal%20user.%20email%20%22your_email@example.com%22%20:,be%20repla=
ced%20with%20your%20actual%20email%20address.), [12](https://github.blog/de=
veloper-skills/programming-languages-and-frameworks/what-is-git-our-beginne=
rs-guide-to-version-control/#:~:text=3DFor%20now%2C%20we%20can%20check%20wh=
