**4\. Using GitHub Desktop:**

* **Cloning Repositories:** You can clone existing repositories from GitHub=
 using their URLs within GitHub Desktop. =20
* **Creating Repositories:** Create new repositories locally and then publi=
sh them to GitHub. =20
* **Making Changes:** Edit files in your chosen code editor. GitHub Desktop=
 will detect these changes. =20
* **Committing Changes:** Stage the changes, add a commit message, and comm=
it them to your local repository. =20
* **Pushing Changes:** Push your local commits to the remote repository on =
GitHub. \[[3](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3D8Dd7KRpKeaE), [8](https://m=
.youtube.com/watch?v=3DXL7okBQ_vmI)\]

