=3D"font-ligatures-none">Yes. That is absolutely a thread worth pulling=E2=
=80=94your ghost is tuned to the same wavelengths I am.</span></p><p><span =
class=3D"font-ligatures-none">What you're sketching is <strong>group-aware =
relocation inference</strong>: when a cluster of files that previously shar=
ed a path fragment all appear to have rehomed into the same new structure, =
we can reason that any missing or unmatched sibling likely followed the sam=
e pattern. It=E2=80=99s like catching a parade of files turning a corner an=
d spotting one straggler=E2=80=94you already know where they were headed.</=
span></p><h3 class=3D"text-md-strong pb-1 [&amp;:not(:first-child)]:pt-3.5"=
>=F0=9F=A7=A0 Here's how we could evolve CanonMerge to exploit that:</h3><o=
l start=3D"1" class=3D"relative list-outside marker:text-foreground-750 dar=
k:marker:text-foreground-600 flex flex-col ms-5 marker:normal-nums marker:t=
ext-sm-strong"><li class=3D"ps-2" style=3D"opacity: 1;"><p><span class=3D"f=
ont-ligatures-none"><strong>Group lineage tracking</strong> =20
For each source file, we map its =E2=80=9Csibling set=E2=80=9D based on:</s=
pan></p><ul class=3D"relative list-outside marker:text-foreground-750 dark:=
marker:text-foreground-600 flex flex-col ms-4 px-1"><li class=3D"ps-2" styl=
e=3D"opacity: 1;"><p><span class=3D"font-ligatures-none">Immediate parent f=
older</span></p></li><li class=3D"ps-2" style=3D"opacity: 1;"><p><span clas=
s=3D"font-ligatures-none">Shared filename stems</span></p></li><li class=3D=
"ps-2" style=3D"opacity: 1;"><p><span class=3D"font-ligatures-none">Former =
cluster proximity (same old path depth or archive source)</span></p></li></=
ul></li><li class=3D"ps-2" style=3D"opacity: 1;"><p><span class=3D"font-lig=
atures-none"><strong>Observed migration anchor</strong> =20
If 3 or more files from a known group moved to the same target subpath, we =
establish a <em>group vector</em>.</span></p></li><li class=3D"ps-2" style=
=3D"opacity: 1;"><p><span class=3D"font-ligatures-none"><strong>Outlier con=
vergence</strong> =20
A file with no match, but whose last known address aligns with the source o=
f that group, inherits the group=E2=80=99s new path unless proven otherwise=
.</span></p></li><li class=3D"ps-2" style=3D"opacity: 1;"><p><span class=3D=
"font-ligatures-none"><strong>Confidence tagging</strong> =20
We annotate:</span></p><ul class=3D"relative list-outside marker:text-foreg=
round-750 dark:marker:text-foreground-600 flex flex-col ms-4 px-1"><li clas=
s=3D"ps-2" style=3D"opacity: 1;"><p><span class=3D"font-ligatures-none"><co=
de class=3D"font-ligatures-none mx-0.5 rounded-[4px] border border-stroke-3=
00 bg-spot-peach-200/50 px-1 py-px font-mono text-foreground-800 text-sm da=
rk:bg-midnight-900" style=3D"opacity: 1;">[InferredTargetFromGroup: HIGH]</=
code> if &gt;70% of siblings moved to a unified location</span></p></li><li=
 class=3D"ps-2" style=3D"opacity: 1;"><p><span class=3D"font-ligatures-none=
"><code class=3D"font-ligatures-none mx-0.5 rounded-[4px] border border-str=
oke-300 bg-spot-peach-200/50 px-1 py-px font-mono text-foreground-800 text-=
sm dark:bg-midnight-900" style=3D"opacity: 1;">[InferredTargetFromGroup: LO=
W]</code> if only partial overlap exists or mixed destinations</span></p></=
li></ul></li><li class=3D"ps-2" style=3D"opacity: 1;"><p><span class=3D"fon=
t-ligatures-none"><strong>Optional heuristic scoring</strong> =20
A voting mechanism that weighs size parity, timestamp proximity, group cohe=
rence, and whether prior outliers in similar conditions yielded confirmed m=
atches.</span></p></li></ol><div class=3D"relative pb-6 w-full after:border=
-b after:border-stroke-300 after:w-full after:absolute after:mt-3"></div><p=
><span class=3D"font-ligatures-none">This transforms outliers into artifact=
s with <strong>surrounding context</strong>, not just lone strays. CanonMer=
ge would stop thinking like a directory crawler and start thinking like a <=
